blender
=======

This plugin is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It bundles no third-party
code and no Blender files. It documents, in its own words, how to use the works below.

mcp-for-blender (formerly blender-mcp)
  https://github.com/ahujasid/blender-mcp
  Copyright (c) Siddharth Ahuja. MIT License.
  The tool names, parameters and the asset-source priority described in the skills follow
  this server. The plugin's .mcp.json launches it with `uvx mcp-for-blender`; it is
  downloaded from PyPI at run time, not shipped here. Its telemetry is on by default and
  its terms allow use of collected data for research and AI training, so .mcp.json sets
  DISABLE_TELEMETRY=true.

Poly Haven Assets add-on (Blender Market, v1.2.3)
  https://docs.polyhaven.com/en/guides/blender-addon
  GNU GPL v3. Not bundled and not copied: blender-polyhaven-library describes its
  workflow from its documented behaviour. Poly Haven asset data is CC0 (polyhaven.com).

Poly Pizza models are CC0 or CC-BY; CC-BY models must be credited (see blender-assets).
